  "result": "I added `wrapText(text, width)` in `src/cli/wrap.ts` and committed it. `npm run fast` passed.\n\n- **Behaviour:** It wraps at word boundaries, so a word that fits (including one exactly `width` long) is never split. Runs of whitespace collapse to one space, and empty text gives `[]`. A word longer than `width` is broken into `width`-sized pieces, which is my reading of the spec, since it didn't cover that case.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/wrap.test.ts` uses `node:test` and covers wrapping, exact-width words, whitespace and empty input, and over-long words.\n- **Shard weight:** I added the new test file to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs` with a weight of 0.1. That is a guess, since the file hasn't run in CI yet.\n- **Commit title:** The convention says to end it with the task id in parentheses, but no task id was in the brief. The commit is `7f55ce9 Add wrapText word wrapping to the CLI` with no id. If you give me the id, I can amend the title.",
